  "conclusion": "Packed bipolar candidate selection improves complete-HDC scan latency relative to RaBitQ but is nearly the same size, lowers exact top-10 recall, and remains slower and about 20x larger than the embedding-plus-structured-rerank candidate index. Paired bootstrap intervals show no statistically significant NDCG or graph-answer advantage at 50, 100, or 200 candidates. It does not reverse the HDC no-go decision."
